                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "const rows = data.rows.map((row) => ({\r\n          date: String(row.date ?? ''),\r\n          count: Number(row.count) || 0,\r\n        }));\r\n        const chart = document.getElementById('chart');\r\n        while (chart.firstChild) chart.removeChild(chart.firstChild);\r\n        rows.forEach((row, i) => {\r\n          const h = Math.round((row.count / max) * 140);\r\n          const isToday = i === rows.length - 1;\r\n          const showTick = i % 3 === 0 || isToday;\r\n          const col = document.createElement('div');\r\n          col.className = isToday ? 'col today' : 'col';\r\n          col.title = row.date + ': ' + row.count;\r\n          const bar = document.createElement('div');\r\n          bar.className = 'bar';\r\n          bar.style.height = h + 'px';\r\n          const tick = document.createElement('div');\r\n          tick.className = 'tick';\r\n          tick.textContent = showTick ? fmtDay(row.date) : '';\r\n          col.append(bar, tick);\r\n          chart.append(col);\r\n        });"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Replace the innerHTML string template with programmatic DOM construction so every value is assigned through a property that is not an HTML parser: set the row date and count through the title property, the tick label through textContent, the bar height through style.height, and the today marker through className. Remove the innerHTML assignment entirely.",
                "markdown": "Replace the innerHTML string template with programmatic DOM construction so every value is assigned through a property that is not an HTML parser: set the row date and count through the title property, the tick label through textContent, the bar height through style.height, and the today marker through className. Remove the innerHTML assignment entirely."
              }
            }
