          "message": {
            "text": "Attacker-controlled URL reaching the SSRF bridge — Requires further review: src/App.tsx EPG URL field (loadEpg, lines 2600, 2616, 2625-2627, 4840, 5486)\n\nStill open, and the gap is specific: epgUrl (user-typed or from localStorage.doggy_epg_url) has no scheme/host validation and is passed to the bridge automatically on mount, so it is an SSRF sink, but no in-repo code path writes doggy_epg_url from a provider response. Remote-only reachability therefore needs either social engineering or a separate renderer-execution primitive. The bridge itself is confirmed and filed (vuln-0001); what remains unproven is an unattended attacker path into this particular field."
