          "message": {
            "text": "XSS / DOM injection from remote playlist, EPG, series data — Ruled out: src/App.tsx renderer DOM sinks (innerHTML / dangerouslySetInnerHTML / eval / new Function / document.write / src={})\n\nrg over all of src/ returns zero innerHTML, dangerouslySetInnerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, outerHTML, document.write, eval( and new Function( — only URL.createObjectURL at App.tsx:2125. Playlist/EPG/series fields render as React text children (item.name:3922,4317,4975,5175; epg title:3924; ep.title/ep.episode_num:3862) or as <img src>/<video src> attributes. Subtitles additionally strip <[^>]+> before reaching the cue (App.tsx:2262 SRT, :2296 VTT, :2387 SMI) and are rendered as {currentCue.text} text (:4193). The only HTML sink in the whole codebase is usage-stats.html:212 chart.innerHTML, whose interpolated row.date is client-generated (telemetry.js utcDay) and row.count is guarded by typeof === 'number' (telemetry.js:87-90)."
