          "message": {
            "text": "OS command injection — Ruled out: electron/main.js spawn/exec sites (spawnIdleFfmpeg, ffmpeg probes, powershell, nice)\n\nAll nine spawn() calls (main.js:66,72,85,139,194,466,696,917,1133) pass an argv array with the default shell:false; there is no execSync, no exec( and no shell:true anywhere in either tree, so shell metacharacters in a filename cannot be interpreted. The only interpolated string is main.js:74-78 powershell -Command \"Get-Process -Id ${proc.pid}\", where proc.pid is the OS-assigned numeric PID of the just-spawned ffmpeg, not caller data. Residual class not tested: ffmpeg option/protocol injection from a path operand starting with '-' or using a concat:/file: protocol prefix (see the open item on the ffmpeg-pipeline surface)."
