          "ruleIndex": 18,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Command-line-file handling / template breakout — Ruled out: electron/main.js:508-523 and :599-608 process.argv / second-instance commandLine → executeJavaScript injection\n\nfileArg is chosen by a video-extension regex and interpolated through JSON.stringify into a JS source string passed to webContents.executeJavaScript (:515-518, :602-605). The string is compiled as JavaScript, not parsed as HTML, so a </script> breakout is inert; JSON.stringify leaves only U+2028/U+2029 raw, which are legal inside JS string literals from ES2019 onward. Reaching this with attacker bytes requires the ability to launch the app with chosen arguments — an already-local position. Downstream consumer handleFileLoad (App.tsx:1798-1810) only appends the value to the playlist."
