            "text": "SSRF / private-range reach from a hostile playlist entry — Requires further review: Playlist channel URL -> hls.js loadSource / iptv-fetch argument (loopback + LAN reach)\n\nGenuinely blocked, and now partly overtaken. isHlsStream() is a bare url.includes('.m3u8') at src/App.tsx:605 with no host/scheme restriction, so a channel URL pointing at loopback or RFC1918 is handed to hls.js. Loopback reach itself is confirmed by vuln-0001 (the bridge reaches any loopback port with full method/header/body control), and webSecurity:false makes cross-origin bodies readable, so the remaining gap is narrower than when this row was opened: what is NOT established is an in-app renderer PoC, because the app needs a Vite build plus an Electron run and only the two source trees are mounted. Closing it requires launching the packaged app with a hostile M3U against a loopback listener."
