          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/secret-disclosure-csrf-style-cross-origin-reach-of-the-loopback-server",
          "ruleIndex": 29,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Secret disclosure / CSRF-style cross-origin reach of the loopback server — Ruled out: streamToken disclosure (electron/main.js:92,936) to a third party\n\nNamed controls, each tested: (1) ffmpeg sends no Referer at all — token-bearing URL fetched by ffmpeg and by hls.js produced 'referer=-' at the remote receiver; (2) Chromium's default strict-origin-when-cross-origin strips the query, so a token-bearing loopback navigation to a remote origin presented only 'referer=http://127.0.0.1:8933/' with no token; (3) Private Network Access blocks the reverse direction — a public-origin page carrying the exact valid token got 'Failed to fetch' and the loopback server logged no request, while curl with the same token got 200, and the page's requests to a public receiver did arrive; (4) every remote item is addressed with '&transcode=true' hard-coded (main.js:936), so no app-generated URL can reach the redirect branch. Residual local-only exposure is covered by the file-read report, not a separate token leak."
          },
          "locations": [
