          "message": {
            "text": "Argument injection / ffmpeg protocol abuse (CWE-88) — Ruled out: ffmpeg input via req.query.path (fluent-ffmpeg(videoPath)) — protocol/argument injection\n\nTwo named controls. (a) fluent-ffmpeg argv assembly keeps the value as a single element after -i: instrumented _getArguments() for 'concat:/etc/passwd|file:/x', '-i', 'file:///C:/Windows/win.ini', 'http://h/a.mp4 -f lavfi' and a NUL variant — every case produced [\"-i\", <verbatim value>, ...] with no extra elements, so no option smuggling is possible; strace confirmed execve argv for '-8' is [\"ffmpeg\",\"-hide_banner\",\"-nostdin\",\"-i\",\"-8\"] and ffmpeg consumed it as the input URL ('Error opening input file -8'), not as an option. (b) protocol abuse adds no capability over the raw absolute-path read already reported: concat:/subfile: still require fs.existsSync(url) to pass, which fails; concat: additionally only reads the first entry unless the first file decodes; HLS file: segments are rejected by ffmpeg's allowed_segment_extensions; crypto: refused with 'decryption key not set'. The one remaining consequence — ffmpeg fetching an attacker-chosen http(s) URL with arbitrary segment fetches — is the designated iptv-fetch SSRF owner's scope and is not double-reported here."
          },
          "locations": [
