          "message": {
            "text": "Command injection into a string-interpolated shell — Ruled out: spawn('powershell.exe', [... -Command, `...${proc.pid}...`]) (electron/main.js:72-75)\n\nNamed control: the interpolated value is Node's own ChildProcess.pid, which the runtime always exposes as a plain integer. Verified empirically on Node v24.21.0 — a live child reported `typeof pid === \"number\"`, Number.isInteger true, digits-only when stringified, and a failed spawn left pid `undefined` (falsy, so the `if (proc.pid)` guard at line 68 skips the powershell call entirely). No attacker-controlled string reaches this command line; all other spawn sites in main.js (lines 66, 145, 194, 293, 454, 1049, 687, 889) use spawn(binary, [arrayArgs]) with no shell."
