          "message": {
            "text": "Path traversal beyond the user's chosen media file — Ruled out: resolveLocalMediaPath() consumers: get-stream-url, probe-seek-quality, optimize-for-seeking, extract-seek-frame (main.js:179-189, 933/1036/1070/1107)\n\nThese handlers accept a path from the renderer, and under nodeIntegration the renderer already has full fs access (createWindow webPreferences at main.js:568-580: nodeIntegration true, contextIsolation false, webSecurity false), so a caller able to choose filePath can read the same file with fs.readFileSync — no privilege is gained and there is nothing to enforce authorisation against. The one real gap was the direction where the renderer receives a URL a NON-Node client can replay, which is the /stream report (the URL carries the path verbatim at main.js:936, and that route never normalises); fixed there. Enumerated every reachable playlist source that could set a path: local OS file dialog (webUtils.getPathForFile), process argv / second-instance (extension-gated), M3U parsing (only lines starting with 'http'), handleOpenUrl (user-typed) — no remote provider string can become a local path."
