          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/injection-through-ffmpeg-encoder-options",
          "ruleIndex": 34,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Injection through ffmpeg encoder options — Ruled out: optimizeForSeeking opts (gopSeconds/crf/preset) from renderer IPC (main.js:319-323, 1070)\n\nNamed control: gopSeconds passes through Math.min/Math.max with Number() coercion, crf through Number.isFinite(Number(...)), and each is re-stringified with String() into its own argv element (main.js:320-321, 355-370); preset is passed as the value of '-preset' in a separate argv slot, so 'preset' can only ever be one ffmpeg preset name — no shell and no pre-parse. The App.tsx caller (line 866) sends the literal {gopSeconds:1, crf:20, preset:'veryfast'}."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
