            "text": "Prototype pollution / key injection from playlist data — Ruled out: Playlist metadata fields as object keys (category id, React key, favorites identifier, localStorage/progress keys)\n\ngroup-title flows into a `Set`, into `{ id: c, name: c }` objects and into React keys, never through a merge/copy helper. Tested a `group-title=\"__proto__\"` playlist (/workspace/.poc-playlist/proto_test.js): the string is stored as an ordinary Set member and `({}).name` stays undefined, so no prototype is touched. `name` is used only in string concatenation (localStorage keys, episode labels), not as an object path."
