        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/provider-controlled-response-steering-further-fetches",
          "ruleIndex": 39,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Provider-controlled response steering further fetches — No issue identified: Xtream player_api.php login response -> stored credentials and channel fan-out (App.tsx:1667-1728)\n\nEvery subsequent request is built from the user-entered base URL plus the user-entered username/password (the `baseUrl`/`userToUse`/`passToUse` locals captured before the response is read); no field of the login JSON is used to choose a host, path prefix or scheme. `user_info.auth === 1` is the only gate on entering the logged-in state — a hostile provider can of course lie, but it is already the operator of the server the user chose."
          },
          "locations": [
