          "ruleIndex": 40,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential in logs / process command line — No issue identified: Provider credential-bearing stream URLs in console/ffmpeg argv (src/App.tsx:714/744, electron/main.js:750/812/933-936)\n\nXtream stream URLs embed user/pass in the path (App.tsx:1688,1701,1713), so when a remote item is transcoded the URL reaches console.log (App.tsx:714/744), the loopback /stream?path= URL, and ffmpeg argv logged at main.js:812 via ffmpeg(videoPath). No log file is written (no createWriteStream/appendFileSync in main.js) — output goes to the parent console only. Not filed as a distinct vulnerability: requires an already-transcoded remote item, exposure is console-only, and process argv is readable only by the same user (Windows does not expose foreign process command lines to other non-admin sessions here). Root cause is the same as vuln-0005; noted as defense-in-depth in its remediation."
          },
