          "message": {
            "text": "JS template-literal injection via JSON.stringify — Ruled out: electron/main.js executeJavaScript window.__initialVideoInfo (argv template literal, lines 511-524 / 597-606)\n\nJSON.stringify correctly escapes the four template-literal metacharacters (backtick, ${), plus \" and backslash, and emits U+2028/U+2029 as literal ESCAPED chars? Verified by executing the exact template: `C:\\v\\${...}`, `` C:\\v\\`+...` ``, `C:\\v\\\";...`, `C:\\v\\';...`, U+2028, and `</script>` all round-trip as inert string data (marker executions = 0); only the benign filename produced a value. Also no argv input path is attacker-controllable: no custom protocol/deep-link registration, no default-app file-association handling, and media downloads do not supply argv (playback is via file:// / loopback stream URL)."
          },
          "locations": [
