          "message": {
            "text": "Update channel trust / arbitrary code update — Ruled out: electron/main.js auto-updater (main.js:536-565) and restart-and-install IPC (main.js:622-624)\n\nNo setFeedURL/allowPrerelease anywhere in either tree; no package.json/electron-builder config present in the supplied trees, so electron-updater resolves the default GitHub-release provider from the packaged app-update.yml, with NSIS differential signature verification (sha512 + publisherName) enforced by electron-updater. No attacker-reachable code path supplies a feed URL: the updater is only invoked with zero arguments at main.js:539/623. Residual: an attacker who can already write the install directory can edit app-update.yml, which presupposes the FILE_WRITE primitive that the navigation finding already provides, so it is not an independent issue."
