            "text": "CSP enforcement vs nodeIntegration; HTML injection from counter service — Ruled out: electron/usage-stats.html CSP and innerHTML chart rendering (usage-stats.html:5, 212-220)\n\nCSP is default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' (no script-src, so 'self' governs scripts, unsafe-inline is ignored for script). The page's only script is inline at line 182-250, yet it runs because meta CSP is enforced after parse for the inline script in Chromium/Electron file:// documents in practice — verified by the application functioning; regardless, CSP is irrelevant because line 183 does require('electron') and nodeIntegration:true. The innerHTML sink at 212 interpolates only row.date (toISOString slice from a locally generated array) and row.count (countFrom() enforces typeof number), so no attacker-controlled string reaches it. No injection path found."
