            "text": "Node integration in a second window with no navigation guard — No issue identified: electron/telemetry.js openStatsWindow() webPreferences and statistics window navigation (telemetry.js:150-173)\n\nThe statistics window uses nodeIntegration:true, contextIsolation:false with no preload and no navigation guard, the same posture as the main window. It is not an independent exploitable route, though: it loads a fixed local file (usage-stats.html) and the only remote influence is JSON from the counter service, which is rendered with textContent and an innerHTML sink constrained to numbers and generated dates (see the CSP/innerHTML entry). No attacker-controlled string reaches a script sink in that document. The defect is the shared preference pattern, which is already reported for the main window (vuln-0008) and whose multi-part fix covers both windows; recorded here so the duplicate posture is documented rather than silently missed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "electron/telemetry.js openStatsWindow() webPreferences and statistics window navigation (telemetry.js:150-173)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
