          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing IPC sender authorization / confused deputy — No issue identified: Electron IPC handler inventory across main.js and telemetry.js (no sender/origin authorization on any handler)\n\nAll 13 handlers were enumerated: quit-app, restart-and-install, iptv-fetch, get-network-info, get-stream-url, cancel-seek-optimize, probe-seek-quality, optimize-for-seeking, extract-seek-frame, telemetry:get, telemetry:set, creator-stats:login, creator-stats:load. Only the two creator-stats handlers call isStatsSender(); the rest accept any sender. Under the current single-window design this is not an independent finding — the sole application window legitimately needs all of them, and the renderer already holds Node privileges by design so a sender check would add nothing. The impact only becomes real once a foreign origin can occupy a window, which is the reported navigation defect (vuln-0008); the durable fix there is removing nodeIntegration plus a preload allowlist rather than adding per-handler sender checks. iptv-fetch SSRF and the ffmpeg file-path handlers are owned by other agents."
          },
